        "original_id": "c0eb731e-3f7e-56e7-9a15-6bc01f37527b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Evert, Mara Santangelo, Nathalie Dechy\n- Events: 1974 John Player Tournament, 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles\n- Roles: defending champions, singles title winner, professional tennis players\n\nFacts:\n- Chris Evert was born on December 21, 1954, and she is a former World No. 1 professional tennis player from the United States.\n- Chris Evert was known as Chris Evert Lloyd from 1979 to 1987.\n- Mara Santangelo was born on June 28, 1981, and she is a former professional tennis player from Italy.\n- At the 1974 John Player Tournament, first-seeded Chris Evert won the singles title and earned £1,750 ($4,200) in first-prize money.\n- At the 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles, Nathalie Dechy and Mara Santangelo were the defending champions.\n- Before the 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles, Nathalie Dechy retired from tennis and could not defend the title.\n- At the 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles, Mara Santangelo chose not to participate.",
